# Owner secrets for llm-wiki-km (#417 + #418, Browser ingress contract #422).
# Install as /etc/llm-wiki-km/owner.env owned by root:llmwiki with mode 0640
# (service user reads it via the systemd unit; it never enters Git, the
# image, a backup artifact, or the browser).
#
# Copy-and-configure contract: a supported Mode 1 profile needs ALL of the
# deployment + owner ingress settings below. The application cross-validates
# them at startup (fail-fast) and on every readiness read (NOT_READY instead
# of a fake SUPPORTED), so a missing or mismatched line can never report a
# working remote Browser session that does not exist.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Profile A (bounded): private HTTP over an encrypted tunnel (preferred when
# no private TLS termination exists). Transport encryption comes from the
# private network / VPN / overlay itself (WireGuard / Tailscale / SSH tunnel).
# Plain HTTP over a public or untrusted LAN is NEVER supported. Because the
# Browser ingress scheme is http, the cookie transport MUST be non-Secure
# (a Secure cookie would never be sent over remote http and the validator
# rejects that combination instead of reporting a fake-green session).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OWNER_AUTH_ENABLED=true
# OWNER_PASSWORD_HASH=<64-hex-sha256-of-owner-password>
# DEPLOYMENT_MODE=PRIVATE_INGRESS
# DEPLOYMENT_FORWARDER_BINDS=100.64.0.5:8766
# DEPLOYMENT_FORWARDER_TARGET=127.0.0.1:8765
# DEPLOYMENT_BROWSER_ORIGIN=http://100.64.0.5:8766
# OWNER_ALLOWED_HOSTS=localhost,127.0.0.1,100.64.0.5
# OWNER_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:8765,http://127.0.0.1:8765,http://100.64.0.5:8766
# OWNER_COOKIE_SECURE=false
# DEPLOYMENT_MAX_INSTANCES=1
# OPENAI_API_KEY=<provider-secret-when-enabled>
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Profile B (preferred when private TLS termination exists): private HTTPS
# ingress. Terminate TLS on the private ingress (private CA / internal cert),
# forward plain HTTP to 127.0.0.1:8765, and keep the cookie Secure. Replace
# the Profile A lines above with these (same cross-validation rules apply;
# https + OWNER_COOKIE_SECURE=false is rejected as a silent downgrade).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DEPLOYMENT_FORWARDER_BINDS=100.64.0.5:8443
# DEPLOYMENT_BROWSER_ORIGIN=https://100.64.0.5:8443
# OWNER_ALLOWED_HOSTS=localhost,127.0.0.1,100.64.0.5
# OWNER_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:8765,http://127.0.0.1:8765,https://100.64.0.5:8443
# OWNER_COOKIE_SECURE=true
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pure SSH-tunnel access (no host listener): keep DEPLOYMENT_MODE=LOCAL_ONLY,
# enable OWNER_AUTH_ENABLED with the hash above, and forward locally, e.g.
#   ssh -N -T -L 8766:127.0.0.1:8765 <user>@<host-private-address>
# then browse http://localhost:8766. No DEPLOYMENT_BROWSER_ORIGIN is declared;
# the localhost Secure-cookie exception keeps the session working over the
# encrypted tunnel.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
